# Eclipse Mosquitto 2.0.22 — environment schema (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# The compose pins eclipse-mosquitto:2. On 2026-08-29 (research date) that tag
# is a same-day rebuild of the 2.0.22 image (matching push timestamp, but a
# different digest per platform — a base-layer/security refresh, not a new
# mosquitto release; GitHub already has v2.1.x tags, but Docker Hub has not
# published a 2.1 image under any tag yet, so "2" still means 2.0.22).
#
# Source: grep of getenv() across the v2.0.22 tarball (src/, lib/, apps/) and
# the image's docker-entrypoint.sh (docker/generic/docker-entrypoint.sh in the
# eclipse-mosquitto/mosquitto repo, the build used for the non-"-openssl"
# tags). The broker itself calls getenv() exactly once, for SNAP_NAME (snap
# packaging detection, irrelevant in Docker); the only other getenv() calls
# are in the mosquitto_ctrl CLI client (XDG_CONFIG_HOME, HOME), which this
# template does not run. The entrypoint script is two lines — chown
# /mosquitto, then exec the CMD — and reads no environment at all.
#
# This template's compose sets no `environment:` block either: it generates
# mosquitto.conf on the fly via a shell one-liner passed as `command`, then
# runs `mosquitto -c /mosquitto/config/mosquitto.conf`. Every real knob
# (listener, allow_anonymous, persistence, TLS, ACLs, bridges, ...) is a line
# in that conf file, not an environment variable — see @docs below for the
# full directive list.
#
# The one thing genuinely affected by the environment is log timestamps:
# mosquitto formats them with the C library's localtime() (src/logging.c),
# which honors TZ the same way any Linux process does. That is the only item
# below.

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("mosquitto.conf directive reference", https://mosquitto.org/man/mosquitto-conf-5.html)
# ---

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is required. Configuration is the mounted/generated
# mosquitto.conf, not the environment.

# IANA timezone name (e.g. America/New_York). Affects only the local-time
# rendering of log line timestamps (localtime() in src/logging.c); the MQTT
# protocol and stored data are unaffected. Empty defaults to the image's
# built-in UTC.
TZ=
